<http://www.semanticweb.org/mein/ontologies/2024/2/untitled-ontology-17#MentalProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "MentalProperty, when used for decision-making, refers to the collection of intangible assets, including intellectual property, knowledge assets, creative outputs, innovative ideas, cognitive constructs, and personal and cultural heritage, that are considered and evaluated to inform and guide decision processes. In this context, MentalProperty serves as the foundation upon which decisions are made, providing valuable insights, perspectives, and resources that influence the course of action chosen. Decision-makers may assess and leverage MentalProperty assets to address challenges, capitalize on opportunities, mitigate risks, and achieve desired outcomes."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
